// (0.25.5) std's own statics under threads: four threads print at once
// (println), write lines through their own Fmt to a file (Fmt::to_fd:
// std's print buffer, which 0.25.4 let it use without print's lock) and
// allocate (with --check-alloc: the checking allocator's tables, which
// 0.25.4 changed from two threads at once), while main reads stdin
// (read_line's buffer: a static only main reaches, as a thread reaching it
// is refused, sync.global). Every line must come out whole, every line of
// stdin be read once, and no block be reported twice freed.
